\label{thmdvectors}
Let $\mathcal A(\mathcal S)$ be a skew-symmetrizable cluster algebra of rank $n$ with principal coefficients at $t_0$, $x$ be a cluster variable of $\mathcal A(\mathcal S)$ and $d^{t_0}(x)=(d_1,\cdots,d_n)^{\top}$ be the $d$-vector of $x$ with respect to ${\bf x}_{t_0}$. Then $d_k=-1,0$ or $d_k>0$ for each $k=1,2,\cdots,n$ and

(i). if $d_k=-1$, then $x=x_{k;t_0}$;


(ii). if $d_k=0$, then there exists a cluster ${\bf x}_{t^{\prime}}$ containing both $x$ and $x_{k;t_0}$.

